cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Phi-Genesis or report results from this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Phi-Genesis: Spectral Research on the Sierpiński Gasket"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zaprudnov"
    given-names: "Evgeny"
    email: "evgeniyzaprudnov@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "RFT-SIRM"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RFT-SIRM/Phi-Genesis"
url: "https://rft-sirm.github.io/Phi-Genesis/"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational and formal research on Sierpiński-gasket graph
  Laplacians, signed Z2-flux boundary conditions, spectral decimation, and
  numerical spectral evidence. The repository records finite-level exact
  calculations, numerical experiments, preregistered statistical audits,
  Lean formalization work, and unresolved research questions. Numerical
  observations and fitted mass-index patterns are not presented as universal
  theorems or established predictive physical laws.
keywords:
  - Sierpiński gasket
  - spectral graph theory
  - graph Laplacians
  - spectral decimation
  - Z2 flux
  - reproducible research
  - Lean 4
